---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="About" description="A technical professional working across systems, infrastructure, AI, automation, and software.">
	<div class="about page">
		<header class="about-header">
			<h1>Interested in how technology holds together.</h1>
			<p>I'm Huzaifa. I work across infrastructure, cloud systems, applied AI, automation, developer tooling, and software engineering, usually on problems that sit somewhere between those boundaries rather than neatly inside one of them.</p>
		</header>
		<div class="about-body">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>How I approach the work</h2>
				<p>I am most interested in problems that require both a systems view and attention to implementation. The useful questions are often not just whether something works, but how it behaves under pressure, how people interact with it, what can be simplified or automated, and where human judgment still matters.</p>
				<p>I care about building technology that is understandable, resilient, and practical. That might mean designing infrastructure, improving a developer workflow, introducing an AI-enabled process, automating operational work, or helping a team make a technical decision that will still make sense a year later.</p>
				<h2>Areas of practice</h2>
				<ul><li>Infrastructure, cloud, and platform engineering</li><li>Applied AI and practical AI enablement</li><li>Automation, internal tools, and developer experience</li><li>Solution design, software engineering, and technical leadership</li></ul>
				<h2>Outside the work</h2>
				<p>A lot of the same curiosity carries into the things I spend time on outside work: Linux, developer environments, keyboards, gaming, music, software, and technology more broadly. I also spend a lot of time reading and learning about space, astronomy, and astrophysics, mostly because few subjects make the scale and complexity of the world feel quite as tangible.</p>
				<p>This site is where I write about the things I am learning, building, experimenting with, and thinking through.</p>
			</div>
			<aside class="side-note"><p class="meta">This site</p><p>A personal knowledge garden for useful notes, project records, and experiments in public.</p></aside>
		</div>
	</div>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
	.about { padding-top: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 8rem); padding-bottom: 6rem; }
	.about-header { max-width: 49rem; padding-bottom: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem); }
	.about-header h1 { max-width: 13ch; margin: 0.35rem 0 0.8rem; font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.3rem); line-height: 0.93; letter-spacing: -0.075em; }
	.about-header > p:last-child { max-width: 56ch; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.5; }
	.about-body { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 43rem) 14rem; justify-content: space-between; gap: 4rem; }
	.side-note { align-self: start; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.5; }
	.side-note p { margin: 0; }.side-note p + p { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
	@media (max-width: 850px) { .about-body { display: block; } .side-note { margin-top: 2rem; } }
</style>
